**Joris Van den Bossche ([@jorisvandenbossche](https://github.com/jorisvandenbossche)) wrote:**

@zzzeek the code snippet above (using `meta = MetaData(engine, schema=schema); meta.reflect(only=[table_name], views=True)`) is indeed from the pandas code inside `read_sql_table` (see https://github.com/pydata/pandas/blob/master/pandas/io/sql.py#L355)

So we should better change this to `meta = MetaData(engine); meta.reflect(only=[table_name], views=True, schema=schema)`?
